# Unit26
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit26核心词汇

predominant/prɪˈdɑːmɪnənt/占主导地位的/English is predominant in business.
prejudice/ˈpredʒudɪs/偏见/We should fight against prejudice.
preliminary/prɪˈlɪmɪneri/初步的/The preliminary results are promising.
premise/ˈpremɪs/前提/The argument is based on a false premise.
presumably/prɪˈzuːməbli/大概/Presumably, he will arrive tomorrow.
prevail/prɪˈveɪl/盛行/Justice will prevail in the end.
primarily/praɪˈmerəli/主要地/The book is primarily for beginners.
primitive/ˈprɪmɪtɪv/原始的/The tribe lives a primitive life.
probe/proʊb/探查/Scientists sent a probe to Mars.
profound/prəˈfaʊnd/深刻的/The book had a profound impact.
progressive/prəˈɡresɪv/进步的/She holds progressive views.
prohibit/prəˈhɪbɪt/禁止/Smoking is prohibited in public.
prominent/ˈprɑːmɪnənt/杰出的/He is a prominent scientist.
prompt/prɑːmpt/迅速的；促使/The news prompted a debate.
propaganda/ˌprɑːpəˈɡændə/宣传/The government used propaganda.
proportion/prəˈpɔːrʃn/比例/A large proportion lives in cities.
propose/prəˈpoʊz/提议/He proposed a new plan.
prospect/ˈprɑːspekt/前景/The prospects for growth are good.
prosperity/prɑːˈsperəti/繁荣/The country enjoyed prosperity.
protest/ˈproʊtest/抗议/Thousands joined the protest.
provoke/prəˈvoʊk/激怒/His remarks provoked anger.
pursue/pərˈsuː追求/He pursued his dream.
qualify/ˈkwɑːlɪfaɪ/有资格/She qualifies for the scholarship.
quote/kwoʊt/引用/He quoted a famous saying.
radical/ˈrædɪkl/激进的/The government proposed radical reforms.
rage/reɪdʒ/愤怒/He was filled with rage.
random/ˈrændəm/随机的/The numbers were selected at random.
range/reɪndʒ/范围/There is a wide range of products.
rank/ræŋk/等级/She ranks first in her class.
ratio/ˈreɪʃioʊ/比率/The ratio of boys to girls is 3 to 2.
rational/ˈræʃənl/理性的/We need a rational approach.
raw/rɔː/生的/The factory needs raw materials.
react/riˈækt/反应/How did she react to the news?
realm/relm/领域/He made contributions to the realm of science.
reasonable/ˈriːznəbl/合理的/This is a reasonable request.
rebel/ˈrebl/反叛/The people rebelled against the tyrant.
recall/rɪˈkɔːl/回忆/I can't recall his name.
recognition/ˌrekəɡˈnɪʃn/认可/She received recognition for her work.
recommend/ˌrekəˈmend/推荐/I recommend this book.
recover/rɪˈkʌvər/恢复/She recovered quickly from the illness.
recruit/rɪˈkruːt/招聘/The company is recruiting new staff.
refer/rɪˈfɜːr/参考/Please refer to the handbook.
reflect/rɪˈflekt/反映/The results reflect the quality of teaching.
reform/rɪˈfɔːrm/改革/The government introduced reforms.
refugee/ˌrefjuˈdʒiː/难民/The camp provides shelter for refugees.
regime/reɪˈʒiːm/政权/The regime was overthrown.
register/ˈredʒɪstər/注册/You need to register for the course.
regulate/ˈreɡjuleɪt/管理/The government regulates banking.
reinforce/ˌriːɪnˈfɔːrs/加强/The evidence reinforces his argument.
reject/rɪˈdʒekt/拒绝/She rejected his proposal.
